    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Fenelon Properties are delighted to bring to the market 6 Church Road, Newtownmountken-nedy, a deceptively spacious three-bedroom semi-detached home occupying a substantial site in a highly convenient village-centre location.\r\nExtending to approximately 106 sq.m. (1,141 sq.ft.), the property offers considerably more accommodation than its frontage might initially suggest, with living space arranged over two floors. While the property would benefit from modernisation, it has been well maintained and offers excellent potential for a purchaser to upgrade and create a very appealing family home.\r\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hall, a particularly generous living room, kitch-en/diner, lean to storage room, ground-floor bathroom and a large ground-floor bedroom. Up-stairs, there are a further two well-proportioned bedrooms.\r\nOne of the property's strongest features is its substantial east-facing rear garden. Extending well beyond the house and bordered by mature hedging and established planting, the garden offers excellent outdoor space and a high degree of privacy, backing towards Season Park Wood.\r\nThe generous site also presents obvious potential to extend or further develop the existing property, subject to the necessary planning permission. There is precedent for infill develop-ment within the surrounding area; however, prospective purchasers should satisfy themselves independently regarding any development potential.\r\nChurch Road enjoys an exceptionally convenient position within walking distance of the cen-tre of Newtownmountkennedy. The village offers an excellent range of everyday amenities including Dunnes Stores, cafés, pharmacy, schools, churches and sporting and recreational facilities.\r\nThe property is also ideally positioned for commuters, with the N11/M11 only minutes away, providing convenient access north towards Bray, Dublin and the M50 and south towards Wicklow. Greystones and Delgany are also within easy reach, while regular bus services (131, 133, 45A, L1) connect the village with surrounding towns and Dublin.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment with Fenelon Properties.\r\n\r\n* Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs/ floorplans provide for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation:\r\nEntrance Hall – 1.19m x 1.13m\r\nEntrance porch providing access to the main living accommodation.\r\nLiving Room – 4.03m x 6.43m\r\nA particularly spacious reception room positioned to the front of the property, offering gener-ous living and entertaining space. Laid with carpet. Dual aspect.\r\nEat-In Kitchen – 4.34m x 3.63m\r\nGenerously sized kitchen with space for everyday dining and access through to the sun room and inner hallway. Overlooking rear garden. Ample counterspace. Rayburn cooker.\r\nStorage/Utility – 1.17m x 4.67m\r\nRunning alongside the kitchen and providing an additional light-filled space overlooking the garden.\r\nBathroom – 1.95m x 2.19m\r\nTiled floors and walls. Shower unit (electric Mira) with tiled surround and glass screen. Wc and whb.\r\nBedroom 1 – 5.80m x 2.70m\r\nGenerous ground-floor double bedroom with fitted storage and laid with carpet.\r\nFirst-Floor Landing\r\nProviding access to the two upstairs bedrooms. Carpet.\r\nBedroom 2 – 4.59m x 3.29m (front)\r\nLarge double bedroom with fitted storage. Carpet.\r\nBedroom 3 – 3.57m x 3.05m\r\nCarpet with fitted storage.\r\nOutside\r\nFront Garden:\r\nThe property is approached through a mature and well-established front garden, predominant-ly laid in lawn with a variety of shrubs, hedging and colourful planting. A pedestrian pathway leads to the front entrance, while off-street parking is provided to the left-hand side of the property. Mature boundaries provide a pleasant degree of screening and privacy from the road.\r\nRear: The substantial east-facing rear garden is a particularly attractive feature of the property. Predominantly laid in lawn and surrounded by mature hedging, trees and established plant-ing, it provides considerable outdoor space and enjoys a pleasant leafy outlook towards Sea-son Park Wood.\r\nGiven the size of the site, there may be potential for extension or further development, subject to planning permission and all necessary consents.\r\nBlock built shed – 2.43m x 4.67m\r\nShed used for storage purposes\r\n\r\n* Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs/ floorplans provide for guidance only."
      },
      {
